#X msg 130 462 @file;
#X text 270 462 Path file to granulate. Only WAV and AIFF formats are
supported. Type: symbol.;
#X msg 130 504 @gdelay;
#X text 270 504 Delay parameter that causes grain calculations to pause
between grains. Type: int. Units: 'ms'. Default value: 0\. Min value:
0\.;
#X msg 130 561 @gdur;
#X text 270 561 Grain duration. Type: int. Units: 'ms'. Default value:
30\. Min value: 1\.;
#X msg 130 603 @goffset;
#X text 270 603 Offset parameter that controls grain pointer jumps
between enveloped grain segments. Type: int. Units: 'ms'. Default value:
0\. Min value: 0\.;
#X msg 130 660 @gramp;
#X text 270 660 Grain ramp. For values of @gramp greater than zero
\, a linear envelope will be applied to each grain. If @gramp = 100
\, the resultant grain "window" is triangular while @gramp = 50 produces
a trapezoidal window. Type: int. Units: '%'. Default value: 50\. Range:
1\...100\.;
#X msg 130 747 @random;
#X text 270 747 Factor used when setting individual grain parameters.
This random factor is applied when all grain state durations are calculated.
If set to 0.0 \, no randomness occurs. When @random=0.5 \, a grain
segment of length duration will be randomly augmented by up to +-duration
seconds (i.e. \, a 30 millisecond length will be augmented by an extra
length of up to +15 or -15 milliseconds). Type: float. Default value:
0.1\. Range: 0\...0.97\.;
#X msg 130 880 @stretch;
#X text 270 880 Stretch factor used for grain playback (1 - 1000).
Granular synthesis allows for time-stetching without affecting the
original pitch of a sound. A stretch factor of 4 will produce a resulting
sound of length 4 times the orignal sound. The default parameter of
1 produces no stretching. Type: int. Default value: 1\. Range: 1\...1000\.;
#X msg 130 998 @voices;
#X text 270 998 Number of simultaneous grain "voices" to use. Type:
int. Default value: 1\. Range: 0\...200\.;
